          "text": "RAB31 is overexpressed in gastric cancer tissues and its overexpression is associated with poor survival outcomes in patients."
        },
        {
          "text": "Silencing RAB31 inhibits gastric cancer cell proliferation, promotes cell cycle arrest, enhances apoptosis, and reduces tumor growth in vivo."
        },
        {
          "text": "RAB31 interacts with GLI1 to regulate gastric cancer cell proliferation and apoptosis through the GLI1 signaling pathway."
        },
        {
          "text": "MicroRNA-30c-2-3p regulates the RAB31/GLI1 pathway by targeting the 3′-untranslated region of RAB31, thereby influencing gastric cancer cell growth and apoptosis."
        },
        {
          "text": "The miR-30c-2-3p/RAB31/GLI1 axis represents a potential therapeutic target for the treatment of gastric cancer."
        }
      ]
    },
