          "text": "CPCGI exerts its neuroprotective effects in Alzheimer's disease by inhibiting the activation of the p38 mitogen-activated protein kinase (MAPK)/NF-κB signaling pathway."
        },
        {
          "text": "CPCGI improves behavioral symptoms associated with Alzheimer's disease in rats, such as sucrose preference and immobility time, which are indicative of depressive-like behaviors."
        },
        {
          "text": "CPCGI reduces oxidative stress markers, including malondialdehyde (MDA) and reactive oxygen species (ROS), while enhancing superoxide dismutase (SOD) activity in the hippocampus of Alzheimer's disease rat models."
        }
      ]
