      "title": "Beyond tumor necrosis factor receptor: TRADD signaling in toll-like receptors",
      "claims": [
        {
          "text": "Tumor necrosis factor receptor 1-associated death domain protein (TRADD) is essential for TNFα-induced apoptosis and NF-κB activation in vitro and TNFα-mediated inflammatory responses in vivo."
        },
        {
          "text": "TRADD is required for the ubiquitination of receptor-interacting protein kinase 1 (RIP1) in the TNFR1 complex, which is critical for NF-κB activation."
        },
        {
          "text": "TRADD plays a crucial role in Toll-like receptor (TLR) signaling, particularly in the TRIF-dependent pathway, and is involved in cytokine production in response to TLR3 and TLR4 ligands."
        },
        {
          "text": "TRADD is indispensable for the formation of follicular dendritic cell clusters and germinal center formation in the spleen, which are essential for adaptive immune responses."
        },
        {
          "text": "TRADD is not involved in Fas-mediated apoptosis or IFNγ-induced signaling, indicating its specificity for certain signaling pathways."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
